This game looks like a group diploma project at the IT department. It’s cool as a diploma project and first experience. But to sell it for 25 euros! Are you out of your mind?

I would love to recommend this game, the art style and concept is great.
This game is merciless every aspect of this game is so difficult it takes all the fun out of playing. Enemies constant advantage gets tiring quickly i.e { enemies hitting you without hitting you, moving twice your speed at all times, and always stopping your attacks.}
There is a lot to like about this game but the difficulty just simply takes the fun out of it, if you're okay with constantly dying or running through areas countless times just to clear a map section then this is right up your alley.

I have played all of the Tiny Troopers games and this brand new installment in the series BARELY deserves a positive review, mostly because the game disappointed me big time.

PROS
- Visually pleasing (a clear graphics upgrade from previous titles, with better models and diverse environments *not only one*);
- There are indoor levels and outdoor 'in-motion' levels (with helicopters, boat or train *but you do not control them*);
- One or two minor bugs in the entire play-through (flawless performance overall);
- Very well structured upgrade system (especially for secondary weapons and special abilities).

Neither Pros, nor Cons
- Story is represented by 6 chapters, but frankly the story does not immerse the player in any aspect (you can ignore it and skip cut-scenes, it does not matter);
- The jokes/comedy is bland at best and the voice acting is cringe (just like the other games *being a matter of taste, I will not consider this a con*).

CONS
- Primary weapons are boring, especially if they are not fully upgraded;
- AI path-finding is terrible and getting stuck in invisible things happens (just like in the other games);
- Game is grindy and very repetitive in terms of content;
- WHERE ARE THE HUMVEE MISSIONS? WHERE ARE THE MISSIONS IN WHICH YOU NEED TO DESTROY LIVE TANKS? WHERE IS ZOMBIE MODE? So instead of adding new types of content (modes/missions/etc), you decided to cut content that was present in the older titles. Not a great move.

Buy when it is at least at 50% off.

The game is pretty decent at best, but transferring over save data from one device to another does not seem to work.

I recently switched to a brand new pc and when it came time to transfer all of my backed up save data, for games that don't support cloud saves, to it and test things out, this game would give me an error screen saying that the data "did not load properly" forcing me to reset.

That's 4 hours of progress that I'll never get back. And I only had two characters left to unlock too which stings even more... ;_;

It's really fun! 
4 different areas with 4 levels;
1 boss fight;
 And I loved that little train!

Not my usual cuppa tea. I like match 3 games, but this one lacks engagement. Despite its sequel, Murder by Moonlight 2 - Crimson Night which has story engagement, nice music and cute match 3 objects, this one lacks something. I don't know. Maybe I just don't like werewolves or simple the way of the game. Even so, if you are looking for match 3 games, this is a game for you.

PROS:
- Interesting story;
- Varied match 3 games;
- Simple Hidden Objects;
- Easy to learn mechanics.

CONS:
- The music is a bit annoying for my tastes;
- Cannot use more than one aiding weapons;
- Lack of player engagement.

If you are looking for match 3 games with werewolves, this is a game for you. I must say pass, because I prefer the vampire one. The cute objects and music in those match 3 games are a delight!

