I wish I had a third option of Yes and No at the same time. This story is a bit Faulkner in terms of chronology and Harold Pinter in terms of characters (day to day characters with a bit of a mystery behind them). 

There is something happening (illness, obsession, perversion), something that happened in the past (a party, teacher, students, sexual outfits) and something that will happen in the future (a one-hand bald man talking about a "harvest"). 

The story did get me a bit interested. I wonder what happened that made this boy, Robert, live in misery or as a recluse. He is absolutely afraid of girls and, for this, he needs to take medication. [spoiler]But, after a few daily tasks, he needs to meditate and he is using the sexual magazines. I was like "Boy, those are bad for you!" And the thing that set me off was that the cat is fetching him these magazines![/spoiler]

PROS:
- Nice graphics and chilling music;
- Wonderful character representations;
- Choice-making and Inventory Items to Drop, Apply, Explore, Read;
- Fragmented chronology;
- Intriguing plot (players want to know more);
- Game lets players discover how to play mini-tasks.

CONS:
- The [spoiler]balloon[/spoiler] sounds scared me (too loud);
- Players have to click on the arrow to read the next text (try to make players click anywhere on the screen - that would be useful);
- No achievements;
- I would prefer a disclaimer or banner before the Main Menu or after the New Game where players are made aware that the game contains sexual images, allude to sexual perversions or contain sensible matters.

With this said, I wish the dev team good luck in crafting the second chapter. I have to say that I want to know what happened and what will happen to Robert. [spoiler]Would he get over his illness? Would he escape the madman's "harvest"? Would he befriend Holly (his neighbour)? Would he break free from the magazines?[/spoiler]

